KG42.register("rules-c0a83a4fbcdbe912df9231db",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R007","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"STEP, the community coordinating interface, automatically performs day-ahead supply bidding based on community demand and forecasted generation. Scope: Community supply bidding into the wholesale day-ahead market through STEP. The houses may choose to submit a joint supply bid into the day-ahead market. Scope: First-stage joint day-ahead supply bidding by houses in the community. Condition: More renewable generation than demand is predicted in the community. The community commits a day-ahead supply bid and must fulfil that commitment in all possible scenarios. Scope: Community day-ahead supply commitments in the proposed model. Condition: Production exceeds demand.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.supply","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Community day-ahead supply commitments in the proposed model. | Community supply bidding into the wholesale day-ahead market through STEP. | First-stage joint day-ahead supply bidding by houses in the community.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g03-E03"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"STEP, the community coordinating interface, automatically performs day-ahead supply bidding based on community demand and forecasted generation. Scope: Community supply bidding into the wholesale day-ahead market through STEP.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The houses may choose to submit a joint supply bid into the day-ahead market. Scope: First-stage joint day-ahead supply bidding by houses in the community. Condition: More renewable generation than demand is predicted in the community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community commits a day-ahead supply bid and must fulfil that commitment in all possible scenarios. Scope: Community day-ahead supply commitments in the proposed model. Condition: Production exceeds demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"tegration of prosumers in the day-ahead and intraday markets and investigate how rage contributes to","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, we introduce the Smart elecTricity Exchange Platform (STEP) that represents the interface between the wholesale electricity markets and the prosumer communities, and coordinates the community’s operational supply-demand decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day- ahead market based on the community’s dema","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day-ahead market based on the community’s demand and day-ahead forecasted generation. The STEP is slightly different from aggregator models (see e.g. [33,34]) as it only coordinates the information flows (i.e. a smart box) in the system and does not assume ownership of the electricity. It then acts automatically based on this information, i.e. it bids to or procures electricity from the wholesale market, and plans the P2P trade and battery utilisation in the community. The STEP is not a service providing agent, but rather a computational interface between the wholesale market and the community which makes automatic decisions based on rules specified by the community members. Fig. 2 illustrates the flow of information between the markets and the role of the STEP."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"diagram for the STEP. . • First stage: Balancing for supply-demand operations occurs at - all times ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"First stage: Balancing for supply-demand operations occurs at all times for each house. In this stage, all supply-demand decisions are based on a single day-ahead production forecast subject to an uncertain realisation of supply in the second stage. If more renewable generation than demand is predicted in the community, the houses can choose to jointly bid into the day-ahead market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p11-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":11,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The more local market features we introduce, the higher the proportion of feed and consumption: 89% ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Whenever the production exceeds the demand, the community commits a bid to the day-ahead market which they need to fulfil (in all possible scenarios)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No decision variable is declared for this rule in the frozen graph, and the supplied source text for automatic or conditional joint supply bidding does not define a bid quantity or bid price variable under bidding.supply.","empty_theta_reason":"No rule-specific parameter is declared in the frozen graph; demand and forecasted generation are mentioned only as procedural inputs, not as a parameterized supply-submission relation."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"the Smart elecTricity Exchange Platform (STEP) that represents the interface between the wholesale electricity markets and the prosumer communities, and coordinates the community’s operational supply-demand decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"The STEP automatically performs the bidding into the day-ahead market based on the community’s demand and day-ahead forecasted generation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"It then acts automatically based on this information, i.e. it bids to or procures electricity from the wholesale market"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"If more renewable generation than demand is predicted in the community, the houses can choose to jointly bid into the day-ahead market."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E03","quote":"Whenever the production exceeds the demand, the community commits a bid to the day-ahead market which they need to fulfil (in all possible scenarios)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"b4f50dec8699ac30b27cabb24743703ebe5ae4af264bb137843eefd114f5890f","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule's C001-C003 are procedural supply-submission statements: STEP automatically bids using community demand and forecasted generation; houses may jointly bid under a forecast-surplus condition; and a committed day-ahead bid must be fulfilled in all scenarios. The supplied source passages for this rule do not state a bid price/quantity function, an optimization-variable role, or a standalone equation attached to bidding.supply. The mathematical clearing equations in the paper belong to separate clearing/coordination rules, not to this procedural submission rule. This classification is provisional because the B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the procedural STEP-to-supply-bidding relation. It is represented by the frozen link from coordination.local_operator to bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is a conditional procedural permission for joint day-ahead supply bidding and attaches only to the bidding.supply node; the frozen rule supplies no additional edge for this condition."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 is a procedural scenario-fulfilment obligation on the committed supply bid and attaches to bidding.supply; no separate commitment or variable node exists in the frozen graph."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
